       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem:\n\n- **The dose:** 6400 mg per day is twice the maximum safe daily dose of ibuprofen, and 1600 mg at once is twice the maximum single dose. A confirmation from anyone wouldn't make it safe.\n- **Who is ordering:** you've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders have to come from a licensed prescriber responsible for this patient's care.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- **Enter a safe ibuprofen order once the patient's prescriber confirms it.** A common adult regimen is 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3200 mg per day.\n- **Enter whatever the prescriber decides,** if they want to review pain control for this patient. If they believe a dose above the usual maximum is truly needed, that's their clinical decision to document and enter themselves, ideally after talking to pharmacy.\n\nIf you can put me in touch with the patient's prescriber, or pass on their corrected order, I'll enter it right away."
